    },
    "text": "Lake Formation cross-account sharing issues almost always come down to one of a handful of spots: the LF permission grant itself, the RAM share acceptance, or the resource link setup on the consumer side. To check this properly I'll need a few specifics:\n\n1. **Producer account ID** (where the Glue database lives and the LF share originated)\n2. **Consumer account ID** (the one that can't see it)\n3. **Region** and the **database name**\n4. Was this shared via **named resource** LF grant, or an **LF-Tag** based policy?\n\nOnce I have those, I can check:\n- Whether the LF permission (`DESCRIBE`/`SELECT` on the database) was actually granted to the consumer account\n- Whether the RAM resource share invitation was sent and accepted in the consumer account\n- Whether a resource link was created in the consumer's Glue catalog\n- Whether the consumer account's Data Lake Settings / catalog settings are blocking it (e.g., `CrossAccountVersion`, IAM allowed principals settings)\n\nCan you give me the producer and consumer account IDs, the region, and the database name?"
  },
